  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This soundboard recording captures the Mountain Goats performing twenty-four songs over 110 minutes at the Neighborhood Theatre in Charlotte, North Carolina, on Friday, May 29, 2026 [1][2]. The setlist includes a mix of recent material and deeper cuts, such as “Armies of the Lord” and “Need More Bandages,” which have limited archived performances [1][2]. Notable highlights include “Bride,” a bustout not heard in 186 archived shows, and “Collapsing Stars,” also a bustout from 131 archived shows [1][2]. The performance features spoken introductions and banter, including a story about “No Children” and a solo transition [1]. The recording was taped by Kyle Kennelly and Emerald Green, with sound engineering by Erich Miller [1]. This is the 458th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following their previous archived performance at Manchester Music Hall on May 28, 2026 [2]. The audio quality is consistent with a soundboard feed, providing a clear perspective on the band’s dynamics [1]. Listeners can expect a full-length concert experience that documents the specific lineup and order of tracks played that evening [1][2].",
